 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'of the Teatro Colon in Buenos Aires, and then returned to France, where he died at age 77. Nicolas Zverev Nicolas Zverev (or Zvereff ; ; 1888, Moscow - 24 July 1965 Saint-Raphaël) was a Russian-French dancer and ballet master. He studied at the Moscow ballet class at the theatre school of the Moscow Imperial troupe. In 1912 he was invited by Sergei Diaghilev to his troupe Ballets russes. Zverev participated in the Ballets russes from 1912 or 1913 to 1926. Among his roles were Slave ("Scheherazade", Michel Fokine’s ballet), Cossack Chief (La Boutique fantasque, 1919), one of the men', 'title': 'Nicolas Zverev'}
