 {'idx': 31, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'the USS Florida on Wrightsville Beach, Masonboro Inlet, North Carolina on 10 February 1864. SS Scotia (1847) PS "Scotia" was a paddle steamer passenger vessel operated by the Chester and Holyhead Railway from 1847 to 1858, and the London and North Western Railway from 1859 to 1861. She was built in Blackwall Yard, London by Money and Wigrams in 1847 for the Chester & Holyhead Railway Company for a passenger service between Holyhead and Kingstown (Dún Laoghaire) and Howth. From 1858 to 1859 she was loaned to the Scilly Isles Steam Navigation Company until their new ship the SS "Little', 'title': 'SS Scotia (1847)'}
