 {'idx': 6, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'X11 object called "pixmap". DRI3 provides two operations, and , one to create a pixmap (in "X Server space") from a GEM buffer object (in "DRI client space"), and the other to do the reverse and get a GEM buffer object from an X pixmap. In these DRI3 operations GEM buffer objects are passed as DMA-BUF file descriptors instead of GEM names. DRI3 also provides a way to share synchronization objects between the DRI client and the X Server, allowing both a serialized access to the shared buffer. Unlike DRI2, the initial operation —the first every DRI client must request', 'title': 'Direct Rendering Infrastructure'}
