 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Erythravine Erythravine is a tetrahydroisoquinoline alkaloid found in the plant "Erythrina mulungu" and other species of the genus "Erythrina." Some laboratory research has investigated the biological activity of erythravine, but the relevance to effects in humans is unknown. It has been shown to be a potent nicotinic receptor antagonist in animal models with an IC50 of 6µM at the α7 site and 13 nM for the α4β2 receptor. It appears to have anxiolytic effects in animal models of anxiety. Further studies suggest that the anxiolytic effects are only reproducible with the whole extract of Erythrina Mulungu but not with the', 'title': 'Erythravine'}
