 {'idx': 2, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'proud to be the Raiders, let our voices swell. Sing of praise to our dear high school Southeast High, all hail. </poem> Southeast Whitfield High School Southeast Whitfield High School is a public high school in Dalton, Georgia, United States. It is part of Whitfield County School District. Its colors are maroon, silver, black, and white, and its mascot is the Raider. The school competes athletically in the 6-AAAA Division of the Georgia High School Association (GHSA). Southeast Whitfield County Comprehensive High School (SHS) was established in 1975, with students merging from rivals Valley Point and Eastbrook High Schools. However,', 'title': 'Southeast Whitfield High School'}
 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Stephen Miller Foote Stephen Miller Foote (February 19, 1859 – October 30, 1919) was a United States Army officer in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. He served in the Spanish–American War and World War I, among other incidents and conflicts. Foote was born on February 19, 1859, in La Salle Township, Michigan. He graduated from the United States Military Academy and was commissioned into the Fourth Artillery. Foote was transferred to the Sixth Artillery, and he graduated from the Artillery School at Fort Monroe in 1888. He remained at the school as an instructor until 1891, and from', 'title': 'Stephen Miller Foote'}
