 {'idx': 15, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Jakismani Monastery The Jakismani monastery (, "jak\'ismanis monasteri", also spelled Jaqismani) is a medieval monastic church in Georgia, some southwest of the town of Vale, Akhaltsikhe Municipality, Samtskhe-Javakheti region. It was repopulated by monks in 2010. The name "Jakismani" is a corruption of the Georgian "Jakisubani" (ჯაყისუბანი), "a district of Jaki". The Jakismani monastery is located in the historical province of Samtskhe, within the Georgian-Turkish border zone. It is accessible through a poor road only after crossing the Georgian border checkpoint. The monastery consists of a main church, named after Resurrection, two small chapels (one of them possibly a pastophorium,', 'title': 'Jakismani Monastery'}
