 {'idx': 20, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Mie–Gruneisen equation of state The Mie-Grüneisen equation of state is a relation between the pressure and the volume of a solid at a given temperature. It is used to determine the pressure in a shock-compressed solid. The Mie-Grüneisen relation is a special form of the Grüneisen model which describes the effect that changing the volume of a crystal lattice has on its vibrational properties. Several variations of the Mie–Grüneisen equation of state are in use. The Grüneisen model can be expressed in the form where "V" is the volume, "p" is the pressure, "e" is the internal energy, and "Γ"', 'title': 'Mie–Gruneisen equation of state'}
