 {'idx': 10, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Best, worst and average case In computer science, best, worst, and average cases of a given algorithm express what the resource usage is "at least", "at most" and "on average", respectively. Usually the resource being considered is running time, i.e. time complexity, but it could also be memory or other resource. Best case is the function which performs the minimum number of steps on input data of n elements. Worst case is the function which performs the maximum number of steps on input data of size n. Average case is the function which performs an average number of steps on', 'title': 'Best, worst and average case'}
