 {'idx': 2, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'period 1792–1804 during the wars of the First and Second Coalitions see French Revolutionary Armies." The Grande Armée was originally formed as "L\'Armée des côtes de l\'Océan" (Army of the Ocean Coasts) intended for the invasion of England, at the port of Boulogne in 1803. Following Napoleon\'s coronation as Emperor of the French in 1804, the Third Coalition was formed against him and La Grande Armée turned its sights eastwards in 1805. They left the Boulogne camps late in August and through a rapid march surrounded General Karl Mack\'s isolated Austrian army at the fortress of Ulm. The Ulm Campaign,', 'title': 'Grande Armée'}
 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': "Ney's corps attacked across the river to the north bank. This plugged one of Mack's few remaining escape hatches. Battle of Haslach-Jungingen The Battle of Haslach-Jungingen, also known as the Battle of Albeck, fought on 11 October 1805 at Ulm-Jungingen north of Ulm at the Danube between French and Austrian forces, was part of the War of the Third Coalition, which was a part of the greater Napoleonic Wars. The outcome of this battle was a French victory. During the Ulm Campaign, Napoleon's Grand Army had executed a massive right wheel to trap the Austrian army led by Karl Mack", 'title': 'Battle of Haslach-Jungingen'}
 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': "Battle of Haslach-Jungingen The Battle of Haslach-Jungingen, also known as the Battle of Albeck, fought on 11 October 1805 at Ulm-Jungingen north of Ulm at the Danube between French and Austrian forces, was part of the War of the Third Coalition, which was a part of the greater Napoleonic Wars. The outcome of this battle was a French victory. During the Ulm Campaign, Napoleon's Grand Army had executed a massive right wheel to trap the Austrian army led by Karl Mack von Lieberich. Starting on the Rhine River, facing east, the various French corps arrived on the Danube River, facing", 'title': 'Battle of Haslach-Jungingen'}
