 {'idx': 24, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'in that they can process reflected waves of energy. Vision processes light waves as they travel from their source, bounce off surfaces throughout the environment and enter the eyes. Similarly, the auditory system processes sound waves as they travel from their source, bounce off surfaces and enter the ears. Both systems can extract a great deal of information about the environment by interpreting the complex patterns of reflected energy that they receive. In the case of sound, these waves of reflected energy are called "echoes". Echoes and other sounds can convey spatial information that is comparable in many respects to', 'title': 'Human echolocation'}]

