 {'idx': 11, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Nam River. In the pre-dawn hours of August 17, a North Korean attack hit the 35th Infantry. North Korean artillery fire began falling on the 1st Battalion command post in Komam-ni at 03:00, and an hour later North Korean infantry attacked A Company, forcing two of its platoons from their positions, and overrunning a mortar position. After daylight, a counterattack by B Company regained the lost ground. This was the beginning of a five-day battle by 1st Battalion along the southern spurs of Sibidang, west of Komam-ni. The North Koreans attempted to turn the left flank of the 35th Regiment', 'title': 'Battle of Masan'}
