 {'idx': 14, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'The Voice of Melodic Metal – Live in Atlanta The Voice of Melodic Metal – Live in Atlanta is the fifth solo album of Rob Rock. Recorded at the Atlanta\'s ProgPower USA festival on September 27, 2008. This is the Rob\'s live album. It was released on May 22, 2009 via AFM Records 1. "Garden Of Chaos" (4:52) 2. "First Winds Of The End Of Time" (4:53) 3. "Rock The Earth" (5:29) 4. "In The Night" (6:04) 5. "Slayer Of Souls" (3:43) 6. "Judgment Day" (6:25) 7. "Only A Matter Of Time" (7:58) 8. "This Time Is The Last Time"', 'title': 'The Voice of Melodic Metal – Live in Atlanta'}
 {'idx': 15, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Siege of Retz The Siege of Retz was a conflict between the Holy Roman Empire and the Kingdom of Hungary in 1486. It was part of the Austro-Hungarian War. The Hungarian capture of the town eventually led to the prosperity of its wine industry. After the fall of Laa the Hungarian King Matthias Corvinus turned to Retz. He was accompanied by his son John Corvinus. He divided his army into three branches, one composed of mainly Bohemians, the second of Hungarians and the third of the light cavalry of the Raci. He besieged the town with them on 4 October.', 'title': 'Siege of Retz'}
 {'idx': 16, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'the term "geosynchronous" may be used to mean geostationary. Specifically, geosynchronous Earth orbit (GEO) may be a synonym for "geosynchronous equatorial orbit", or "geostationary Earth orbit". Communications satellites are often given geostationary or close to geostationary orbits so that the satellite antennas that communicate with them do not have to move, but can be pointed permanently at the fixed location in the sky where the satellite appears. A semi-synchronous orbit has an orbital period of half a sidereal day (i.e., 11 hours and 58 minutes). Relative to Earth\'s surface, it has twice this period and hence appears to go around', 'title': 'Geosynchronous orbit'}
