 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Black Bog Black Bog is a raised bog in County Tyrone, Northern Ireland, situated about 17km west of Cookstown. It is one of the two largest intact active bogs in Northern Ireland with hummock and hollow pool complexes and represents one of the best examples of this habitat type in the United Kingdom. The raised bog which covers most of the site contains the full range of characteristic vegetation and structural features associated with this type of habitat and is surrounded by cut-over bog with poor fen. The Black Bog Ramsar site (wetlands of international importance designated under the Ramsar', 'title': 'Black Bog'}
