 {'idx': 36, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'the Arab peoples should be united together in a single state under his leadership. Egypt was briefly united with Syria under the name the United Arab Republic from 1958 until 1961 when Syria abandoned the union. Nasser saw himself as the successor of Mohammad Ali the Great, the illiterate Albanian tobacco merchant turned Ottoman "vali" (governor) of Egypt, who had sought to found a new dynasty to rule the Ottoman empire in the 19th century. Nasser came to embrace pan-Arabism as the best way of justifying a greater Egypt that would stretch from the Atlantic to Indian oceans. After the', 'title': 'Egyptian nationalism'}
